==English==
{{wikidata lexeme|L1043}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*dewk-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|enducen}}, borrowed from {{der|en|la|indūcō|indūcere|t=lead in, bring in, introduce}}, from {{m|la|in}} + {{m|la|dūcō||lead, conduct}}. Compare also {{m|en|abduce}}, {{m|en|adduce}}, {{m|en|conduce}}, {{m|en|deduce}}, {{m|en|produce}}, {{m|en|reduce}} etc. Doublet of {{m|en|endue}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈduːs/|a=GA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈdjuːs/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-induce.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|uːs|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[lead]] by persuasion or influence; [[incite]] or prevail upon.
#: {{syn|en|entice|inveigle|put someone up to something}}
#* {{RQ:Churchill Celebrity|IV|58|The Celebrity, by arts unknown, '''induced''' Mrs. Judge Short and two other ladies to call at Mohair on a certain afternoon when Mr. Cooke was trying a trotter on the track. The three returned wondering and charmed with Mrs. Cooke; they were sure she had had no hand in the furnishing of that atrocious house.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[cause]], [[bring about]], [[lead]] to.
#: {{syn|en|bring about|instigate|prompt|stimulate|trigger|provoke|Thesaurus:incite}}
#: {{ux|en|His meditation '''induced''' a compromise.&nbsp;&nbsp; Opium '''induces''' sleep.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=May 20, 2012|author=Nathan Rabin|work=The Onion AV Club
|title=[http://www.avclub.com/articles/marge-gets-a-job,73723/ TV: Review: THE SIMPSONS (CLASSIC): “Marge Gets A Job” (season 4, episode 7; originally aired 11/05/1992)]
|passage=A mere glance at the plot descriptions of the show’s fourth season is enough to '''induce''' Pavlovian giggle fits and shivers of joy.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To induce the [[labour]] of (a [[pregnant]] [[woman]]).
#* {{RQ:Guardian|date=2014-12-05|author=w:Marina Hyde|title=Childbirth is as awful as it is magical, thanks to our postnatal ‘care’|url=https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2014/dec/05/childbirth-postnatal-care-birth-hospital-cuts|passage=By the time of my third, five months ago, I was a right bossy cow about what I wanted because I knew the drill. For reasons I shan’t bore you with, I got them to '''induce''' me at 39 weeks, at 10am, with the epidural going in first, and it was all a dream. |archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20261013101226/https://www.theguardian.com/commentisfree/2014/dec/05/childbirth-postnatal-care-birth-hospital-cuts|archivedate=13 October 2026}}
# {{lb|en|physics}} To [[cause]] or [[produce]] (electric current or a magnetic state) by a physical process of [[induction]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|logic}} To [[infer]] by [[induction]].
#: {{ant|en|deduce}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To [[lead in]], [[bring in]], [[introduce]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To [[draw on]], [[place upon]]. {{rfex|en}}

